{
  "role": "independent-outcome",
  "decision": "retain-with-limits",
  "candidate": "BODY01 only, retained02, original09 head; Advanced/builder, Maker, Mechanic",
  "basis": "Meaningful net whole-character source gain survives all three eras and both native lighting rigs. Short overlapping breast courses replace the long smooth vertical bib; the segmented armor mass reads closer to the pinned full-bird construction at normal whole-image scale. This is a useful regional increment, not a completed source-aligned three-era target.",
  "gains": [
    "Shorter overlapping breast courses visibly break up the formerly long smooth bib in each paired whole image.",
    "Original09 hooked beak/optic, compact shoulder shields, exposed side mechanisms, stance and talons remain useful; inspected profiles/rear show no obvious new continuity loss outside the breast."
  ],
  "costs": [
    "New broad rounded scallops are oversized, smooth and puffy compared with the source's thin tightly fitted irregular metal.",
    "Exact front neutral-000 exposes a new conspicuous triangular opening at mid-breast plus lower gaps; the old front was continuous. Upper throat-to-breast course change is abrupt. These are construction costs, not a dark-light or color effect.",
    "Inherited smooth broad cap/bill, sparse cheek and hollow rear head remain substantial source gaps.",
    "Maker and Mechanic remain visually very similar; era material and repair histories are much simpler than the pinned era sources."
  ],
  "weighing": "The breast course change is readable without close-up detail and remains useful despite the added gaps and puffiness. Retain the BODY01 increment with those defects recorded; do not substitute it for owner acceptance or claim every viewpoint is improved.",
  "module_recommendations": {
    "BODY01": "retain as loop01 useful progress with limits",
    "HEAD01": "remain excluded; this review evaluates original09 head"
  },
  "top_two_next_major_source_gaps": [
    "Build the source-specific fitted crown/orbit/cheek-to-throat head construction: broad smooth cap/bill and hollow/sparse cheek/head remain the dominant identity gap.",
    "Make the breast a coherent fitted metal shell: thinner crisper irregular courses, close triangular/open seams and blend the upper join, while carrying distinct source-grounded era finish/repair character."
  ],
  "browser_outcome": "All 12 frozen captures show the selected era and both lighting or manual native PNG fallback states. The short-course breast persists in WebGL. Browser neutral has softer flatter metal highlights and exhibit has a hazier lower-contrast response than native; no pixel parity. Advanced optic is lit, Maker/Mechanic dark. Frozen captures are not my own live interaction or runtime reproduction.",
  "claim_statuses": [
